What are Electrophysiology (EP) Devices?
Electrophysiology (EP) devices are sophisticated medical instruments used to diagnose and treat abnormal heart rhythms (arrhythmias) by mapping and analyzing the heart's electrical activity. These systems offer a minimally invasive alternative to traditional cardiac surgery, enabling clinicians to precisely locate and ablate (destroy) the small areas of heart tissue causing the irregular rhythms. The primary device categories that drive the market include EP Ablation Catheters, which hold the largest revenue share at approximately 31%, EP Diagnostic Catheters (~16%), and EP Mapping/Recording Systems (~15%).

